86413042 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(4t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413042 1072 #uuid "7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413042 1074 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=4t-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+4t-1)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2}-2t+4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{4}+4(2)^{3}-{2}^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[24+32-4] \\\\  & =52\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413041 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1069 "q-124867" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the line $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,4]?$" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1072 #uuid "9c8aeb24-90cc-5de9-a270-6cd27812a200" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true] [17592186413043 1074 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt{2}t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,z(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})+8{t}^{3}\\cdot (2)-4{t}^{2}\\cdot (2)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}16{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534173 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0f99d644-a1ad-5b43-b8be-36588f2a8d57" 17592186413006 "answer-207e611c-1715-5848-8636-a148354824ca" 17592186413007 "answer-355201fd-a87c-5acd-a773-040c3348da1d" 17592186413008 "answer-3ea3a4f2-a959-540f-86d2-a526fb567a9f" 17592186413009 "answer-407b1421-300f-5650-8cf7-dd126bc29f0b" 17592186413010 "answer-41ad462e-980a-55e7-8603-ff255c0b0f91" 17592186413011 "answer-5653a3c0-a432-54b1-bd34-3f7fd032cf28" 17592186413012 "answer-5adc34ca-ff1e-5a7e-a58d-e5f402ec7226" 17592186413013 "answer-5b212ba5-4523-505f-abd1-6ed94aa4f312" 17592186413014 "answer-6cf6010e-a80e-5fc9-aa97-fc8be288477c" 17592186413015 "answer-707c6361-9302-5d0e-9948-6d00df2a56db" 17592186413016 "answer-7491be96-5601-5301-a5ca-7f7629fc7e2c" 17592186413017 "answer-7acff49a-3d77-5139-87b8-23f8a83a61d7" 17592186413018 "answer-82a266c0-edf7-5c04-bf6f-54846fdc04bf" 17592186413019 "answer-874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" 17592186413020 "answer-8c8a1d3b-7cc7-56d2-8a